      "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> This PR was drafted with the assistance of Claude Opus 4.6.\n\n## Fix\n\nFixes #50154\n\n### Problem\n\nIn `DeepseekV2DecoderLayer.forward()`, `input_is_sequence_parallel` is determined by:\n\n```python\ninput_is_sequence_parallel = (\n    self.use_sequence_parallel_moe\n    and residual is not None\n    and hidden_states.shape[0] != full_num_tokens\n)\n```\n\nFor small decode batches where `full_num_tokens < tp_world_size` (e.g. 1-3 tokens with TP=4), `reduce_scatter` produces `hidden_states` with the same size as `full_num_tokens` (since `ceil(n/4) == n` when `n < 4`). This makes the shape comparison `False` even when SP is active, so `residual` is never chunked — causing shape misalignment that accumulates garbage across layers.\n\n### Fix\n\n1. Add fallback: also detect SP when `full_num_tokens < tp_world_size`, since scatter is effectively a no-op in this case but SP state is still active.\n2. Use `residual.shape[0] != hidden_states.shape[0]` for the residual chunking decision — more robust than relying on the boolean flag alone.\n\n### Testing\n\n- Aggregated deployment: TP=4, EP=4, DP=2, GLM-5.2-FP8 (744B), `--enforce-eager`\n- Without fix: garbled output on all short prompts\n- With fix: correct generation, gsm8k accuracy ~0.95\n\n### Raw output comparison\n\n**Before (garbled):**\n```\n\"Paris. Paris Paris Paris Paris Paris the the most. Paris and Paris a Paris1140 and41.1,1.0.\"\n```\n\n**After (correct):**\n```\n\"Paris. It is the largest city in France and the country's political, economic, cultural, and commercial center.\"\n```",
